{"kind":"report","text":"# First-use path and acceptance handoff\n\nPlanning only for request d90cd722b5737f25af27dae1e2522f81de6d08dd; root promise 245a80f87a1a96002b7626fe5c9f325fe39b5d55. Source baseline main 38b0b2f2bdb7af6f59076ac3b423741555a7b437. No source edits, installs, tests, application/browser/provider execution, cloud sessions, authority changes or deployment were performed. Local /tmp evidence only.\n\n## Concrete path to adopt\n\nUse one Pages starter, with operator preparation visibly separate from ordinary enrollment. The immediate supported path is an invitation into an already prepared room; it is not a substitute for the still-required empty-to-new-room acceptance.\n\n1. Operator deploys a compatible scope Worker with its own Git host binding, session secret and exact configured register. Operator uses existing `artroom install --plan \u003cservice\u003e --host artifacts --namespace artroom-demo` (or explicitly authorized github.com/account), pins that computed register identity in host settings, then `artroom install --planned`. This is operator work, not an ordinary-user quickstart or a call the starter may make implicitly. Installation authorization itself remains unimplemented.\n2. Authorized founder uses `artroom claim \u003clabel\u003e --handle \u003chandle\u003e`. Native claim retains exact found/seat/first-key requests, confirms directory/membership/rules/destination and makes founder admin. The typed CLI label is output-only, not a recorded shared room name; Page local label is personal context, separate from the generated repository name. Founding alone does not activate an application.\n3. Room admin applies the reviewed Pages preset: activate exact issue/change definitions in rules scope and publish the complete reviewed rules configuration. Actual public acts are `rules.activate` (fields digest/name plus retained definition bytes) and `rules.publish` (approvals, ownerMayReview, checks, labels, extents, optional singleControllerException). Optional checker requirements also need keep-configuration, an enrolled checker key and actual operator-run checking. This first slice can use independent human review without pretending it is a machine check. There is no Pages preset artifact, version, orchestration or --app command yet.\n4. Admin creates a role-scoped invitation with existing `artroom invite \u003chandle\u003e --role member`. Cold CLI user runs installed `artroom join \u003clink\u003e` from a genuinely empty user context; the command makes/keeps the device key and learns full room references from the invitation. Cold browser opens the serving Worker's `/page/`, supplies invitation and creates a local key, then joins. A proposed task-specific invitation screen can combine these supported operations while hiding config/key/schema input; it must respect the invitation's actual origin and role. No raw key transfer is needed for either ordinary enrollment path.\n5. Ready means this enrolled user can read the exact room, see activated issue/change definitions and recorded rules, create and read back an issue, and perform a supported first content contribution. CLI `artroom clone \u003cfresh-target\u003e` obtains its own room-issued read credential and clone; `artroom edit \u003cpath\u003e --file \u003cUTF-8 file\u003e` supplies technical base/digest/size from actual content, opens/proposes a one-file change and attempts merge. Native member lacks change.merge: expected accepted proposal plus explicit unauthorized merge is distinct from publication. An authorized maintainer/admin then requests/obtains any required distinct review and performs merge. Follow actual destination receipt/published commit and read `/site/\u003cdirectory\u003e/HEAD/\u003cpath\u003e`. For a pure initial readiness check the issue readback is sufficient; complete useful-result acceptance still includes the contribution/review/publication, not merely a key, empty scope or UI fixture.\n\nThe empty-to-new-room variant must replace steps 1–4 for the person with a separately adopted creation entry that supplies an authorized register, full pin, handle and Pages preset, then performs native claim and application activation under legitimate admin authority. The current code supplies no such entry for a fresh browser or ordinary fresh CLI key. Do not advertise a name-only new-room quickstart until those seams exist.\n\n## Exact current interface and version inventory\n\n- All current workspace Artroom packages inspected are 0.1.0-dev.1. CLI is private, bin `./bin/artroom.js`, export `.` -\u003e `./src/index.ts`, runtime Node \u003e=22 plus pinned tsx 4.21.0. Commands/store/line are exported; Node fileStore and main are not public exports. Current command dispatcher has install/claim/invite/join/acts/act/log/show/verify/remote/clone/edit/merge/issue/issues. No init/connect/status/publish/app/propose command on main.\n- Client `.` exports signedIntent, secretSigner/webCryptoSigner, ScopeHandle, declaredHandle, httpTransport/bindingTransport, preparation/sendPreparation, session/signed-read and readCredential modules. Actual transport operations are scope found/submit/settle/read/followReceipt/followDuty. This client does not export the old Room connect/generateSigner/onPrepared/resubmit/replay API described in N3/N5. Its settle returns a receipt or not-found, not the proposed B2 universal terminal-absence/preparation contract.\n- Current native founding cohort is register@2 -\u003e directory@2 with membership@2, rules@2, destination@2 (actual claim confirms pins). Do not route through aliases inferred as newest. Main lanes package 0.1.0-dev.1 exports `.` plus definitions/issue.json and definitions/change.json; `.` also exports issueDemo/changeDemo and DEMO_DIGESTS.\n- Main demo issue digest sha256:82a938c8f54ddcac7974ca688ebea7d51c35d2aa70f4e3729965e9f915bc464e; demo change digest sha256:d86c64ae0a570165660a6eb4d75153b8c2f59c9cdaec2ecc789e2c38524a17a2. Full issue sha256:325cb4f33da9deb1a31d85ba0f1456068d4d9d08009978b779aed70cb08e00ad; full change sha256:3f0389ba644e6d58e96a352debcc77d01661ffcf349c6db53d0645c2513eae70. These are definitions, not a versioned Pages preset or proof of its configuration. No demo-JSON export subpath is promised; use exported values only through a released, supported consumer runtime.\n- `/page/` is the scope Worker's embedded app; `/site/\u003cdirectory\u003e/\u003cref\u003e/\u003cpath\u003e` is the delivered rendered publication route. Head reading is latest content, not immutable selected-version completion.\n- Public released package versions/integrities: NONE established. docs/release.md explicitly says earlier-model packaging is inactive, parked, and new-model release is I6 work. docs/cli.md says nothing is published; historical npm E404 was dated evidence, not a fresh registry query. No new registry query was authorized or made. Therefore do not print an install command or claim 0.1.0-dev.1 is obtainable from npm. N3 must provide actual registry release plus outside-consumer lockfile and installed CLI/client proof before cold public-package acceptance. Handed tarballs can be separately qualified development evidence, not completion.\n- Unlanded b8 source request/manifest-composed at 679d7a96d9e25f1ff666969215e820bf91480ffc adds propose \u003cbranch\u003e, manifest-list destination@3/pins and recovery. It preserves the historical REGISTER@2 alias and literal old pins, while its current CLI install consumes NEWEST and founds register@3 automatically; that register creates directory@3/destination@3. Its new propose requires destination@3 and manifest-list active change declaration. No first-use slice may silently activate @3 in an @2 room, promise b8 as delivered main, or create a competing manifest implementation/gate.\n\n## Delivered versus missing authority\n\n| Step | Delivered interface | Missing / owner |\n|---|---|---|\n| Deploy host/register | Planned install and configured-register host boundary; actual host adapters | Provider/operator dispatch, installation permission enforcement and release-bound outsider setup: N5/C1/I3 operator |\n| Fresh ordinary key creates room | Native register found supports policy open or immutable keys allowlist | Supported creation entry/readiness discovery and authorization: C4/N5/027.2. CLI claim first reads register summary; Page allowedClaim also requires summary plus selected room/member handle. Fresh key has no recent signed-entry/root or membership session to authorize that summary. Open founding policy alone does not solve this read seam. Existing register founders list has no supported ordinary invite/add-founder command. Never borrow operator key or invent a readiness method |\n| Application activation | Native rules.activate/publish, retained exact definition bytes and rules state | Reviewed Pages preset bytes/digest/version/default review policy and durable orchestration: 025 + 027.2 with C6/product owner; N5 reconciles authority |\n| Ordinary enrollment | CLI exact saved private join; browser current-context enrollment fence/known answer | Browser invitation landing form and reload-safe exact join recovery: C4/C5/027.2, within existing enrollment custody owner, no generic outbox |\n| Work/source/publication | Issue commands, one-text edit; read-token clone; native review/merge/site | Browser ordinary editing/path correction/review diff remain existing f732/027 owners. b8 branch workflow remains b8. Exact reviewer source/read disclosure under N1; current authenticated literal one-file preview is not a general tree diff |\n| Public packages/starter | Source exports, workspace version, Node launcher | N3 f329 + current d068 owner: reconcile old spec and release tested public packages; owner grants npm/repository publication. I6 release packaging is pending; no registry success asserted |\n| Real cold acceptance/docs | Existing C6/I6/N6 owners | Exact deployed release/current source, independent person and reviewer, help/time/cost, browser and physical accessibility evidence. Recorded Worker answers and signed-POST interceptions prove their labelled boundary only |\n\n## Smallest implementation slice, after named decisions\n\nA. Under 025/027.2, deliver one immutable Pages preset descriptor: exact definition closure, rule configuration and runtime compatibility; no new platform protocol. Reuse native admin rules.activate/publish. Save each exact signed stage before send and accepted fact after; resume original subject/key/ref and verify actual active bytes/rules before marking ready. Scope-specific application orchestration uses the existing owned recovery seam and must not become a generic outbox.\nB. Under C4/C5, add a first-use invitation task screen to `/page/`; ordinary input is invitation and optional personal label, generated key stays private. Reuse actual Page/CLI membership semantics. Do not expose raw config/key/schema as the routine task or import operator authority. Clearly render unavailable/forbidden/expired invitation/readiness states.\nC. Under N3, release and pin the actual current-model packages and a separate minimal starter consumer/lockfile. Supply supported storage/runtime adapter instead of importing private fileStore/cloudflare:test/source paths. The cold CLI entry is actual installed `artroom join \u003clink\u003e` until 027.2's proposed local-preparation/connect vocabulary has its own adopted contract and implementation. Empty folder preserves all files and contains no secret-bearing context.\nD. Before empty-to-new-room implementation, C4/N5/027.2 must adopt the narrow authenticated register-read/eligibility handoff and legitimate creation authority. A link/config assertion cannot itself grant permission. Name the actual participant key, founder-handle source, register policy/pin, preset activation authority and operator cost/retention owner. Implement only that agreed seam; no operator install in ordinary starter setup.\n\n## Concrete decisions for planner/owners\n\n1. Is first release invitation-first into operator/admin-prepared rooms, while new-room creation remains explicit open acceptance, or must empty-to-new-room ship in the same slice? The existing request retains both; invitation success cannot close creation.\n2. Which deployment/register/host is provisioned for outsiders, and which precise interface authorizes a fresh caller's register discovery/founding? Current CLI default keys policy admits only operator key; open policy requires operator creation and still lacks pre-claim read eligibility for a fresh key. No new endpoint is selected here.\n3. Pin the Pages preset and supported @2 or later explicit @3 cohort. Choose rule configuration and reviewer/merger path. Demo script uses zero source approvals/no checks; do not adopt it as default. Native member may propose/review but not merge. Do not silently widen member actions or label maintainer as member. Solo exception needs explicit decision; fixed rules extent still requires approval/controller safeguards.\n4. N3 release owner must provide real registry identifiers, exact versions/integrities/export/runtime evidence and public starter publication authority. Reconcile historical N3 changes-requested spec (6c7b42d0, review2a0294fc) and historical approved N5 design (98c0883f, review1ca27675) against current scopes; neither old Room/v2 protocol is an executable current bootstrap.\n5. Confirm public/private site/source disclosure and retained development-room cost/cleanup responsibility; do not invent room deletion or reuse user's provider credential.\n\n## Cold-user acceptance scenarios\n\n| Scenario | Required observed result |\n|---|---|\n| Empty CLI folder, fresh ARTROOM_HOME, published exact packages | No source/workspace imports; join creates private local device key, exact pinned member/inbox/repository; app readiness independently verifies activated definitions/config. User creates issue, reads it, clones with its own scoped credential, edits supported UTF-8 page; proposal is distinct from merge; qualified reviewer and authorized merger publish actual commit; rendered page matches recorded result |\n| Fresh browser localStorage and same-origin app | Invitation task supplies native room references and enrollment; no operator key/config/schema editing; new local key belongs only to actual admitted user. Readiness/issue readback plus real contribution/review/publication follow. Neither seeded actor fixture nor recorded answers count as hosted success |\n| New-room cold entry | Legitimate discovery/authorization contract first; named user enters name/handle and preset, native found/seat/key, exact admin activation and attach complete. Refused/no authority signs no unauthorized creation; application-ready is false until actual activation and destination founding state are confirmed |\n| Refusal / unavailable | Wrong-origin/incompatible pin/expired or consumed invitation, removed key, unauthorized rules activation, unavailable operator host or missing definition display concrete state and next legitimate action; no false ready/published or role substitution. Backend refusal may be evaluated at a head; no unchanged-head claim without evidence |\n| Lost accepted enrollment / activation reply | CLI repeats original invitation and uses kept key/exact envelope; accepted fact is checked via settle. Application stages retain exact request before send; timeout/not-found/read failure is not permission for new request or success. Current generic CLI/Page lacks durable universal application recovery: implement only owned narrow slice or mark witness blocked |\n| Browser reload after unknown Join | Current in-memory fence is lost and cannot satisfy recovery acceptance. Existing C4/C5 enrollment owner must preserve exact secret-bearing request privately and restore actual room/key/incarnation; retry/settlement must use same request. Changing invitation/settings does not permit a second enrollment under unknown identity. Explicitly record this unmet case until delivered |\n| Local write failure after remote claim/activation | Accepted native room and operation remain discoverable under original private record; user Resume selects known subject without new found, signature or second repository. A separate deliberate new creation never overwrites unknown earlier work. Existing Page claim journal is useful evidence, not full preset completion |\n| Interrupted operator/bootstrap or missing host config | Saved planned install/claim remains original identity; report Waiting for operator configuration with actual action, not ready. No register replan/credential mint/repository duplication from ordinary retry; verify actual configured source/version/host before proceeding |\n| Occupied folder / second room / conflicting context | Files, index and remotes unchanged; resolve explicit room context or stop before transport/token/signing. CLI current global one-room store and clone preflight gaps are 027.2 acceptance, not already delivered. No secrets in attachment metadata |\n| Review state moves / denied source | Reviewer can obtain authorized exact content and retains selected version; missing/different source blocks justified approval. Changing policy/room/incarnation does not silently rebind. Published result remains tied to actual receipt/commit; HEAD UI label alone does not satisfy immutable-version design |\n\nAcceptance owner C6/I6 records full exact release/commit/preset/deployment, actor control, commands, manual/setup/help steps, elapsed/cost bounds, actual publication/refusal/recovery and accessibility findings. One affected-boundary witness plus one justified real hosted smoke, not repeated platform suites. No target of 15 minutes or no-compromise usability is claimed from this read-only handoff.\n\nEvidence locations (static reads): main packages/cli/src/line.ts:8-33,64-90; commands.ts:313-405 (operator install),489-519 (claim setup/read),663-775 (invitation/join),1093-1150 (clone),1273-1339 (edit); store.ts:14-92 and files.ts:19-91 (private/global context); packages/platform/src/register.ts:57-61,119-166,281-300 (pins/policy), membership.ts:150-176 (roles), rules-scope.ts:204-277 (publish/activate), extents.ts:55-83 (fixed rules extent); packages/lanes/{package.json,src/index.ts,src/digests.ts}; packages/client/{package.json,src/index.ts,src/handle.ts:45-70,src/prepare.ts:22-42}; packages/page/src/main.ts:254-302,388-398 and claim.ts:144-155; scripts/demo/rehearse.ts:127-170 (expert/operator + demo activation); docs/{release.md:1-3,cli.md:13-43,page.md:44-83,120-149,pages.md}; plans/006 experience map and task owner map,025 published pages section5 and 027.2 full handoff. CLI story.scope.test.ts explicitly labels Git host, scheduler/clock and memory-store stand-ins; Page doc explicitly states test Worker/recorded-answer capture limits. Historical N3 exact 735 lines,42,599 bytes/SHA93a476a0d3df63fc3fcaa53f7263f76f9a0fcc57a9dd8e02be7effc6bedfac8d; historical N5 exact666 lines/SHAfa219ace8532fe9e5baa75883cd004cf2938ff2a8152214dff30eb14114dc592 retained separately in this /tmp directory. I extracted whole historical files, selectively inspected relevant sections, and fully inspected N3's full changes-requested review; I do not claim a new full historical design review.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:245a80f87a1a96002b7626fe5c9f325fe39b5d55 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:00a6f83a0f12d69721bf0bd026b14608ffac8a31, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0148a0176116a4fb5401c96dbbb813a144b65616, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0357a3c97289e2782ff1264563897f39ecb2ce42, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:03f7bc46d133f1cde1f7936baaaa690a99416b97 and 56 more"}}